DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__lloocckk() function will acquire _l_o_c_k if it is not currently
     owned by another thread.  If the lock cannot be acquired immediately, it
     will spin attempting to acquire the lock (it will not sleep) until it be‐
     comes available.

     The pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__ttrryylloocckk() function is the same as pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__lloocckk()
     except that if it cannot acquire _l_o_c_k immediately it will return with an
     error.

     The pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__uunnlloocckk() function will release _l_o_c_k, which must have
     been previously locked by a call to pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__lloocckk() or
     pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__ttrryylloocckk().

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     If successful, all these functions will return zero.  Otherwise, an error
     number will be returned to indicate the error.

     None of these functions will return EINTR.

EERRRROORRSS
     The pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__lloocckk(), pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__ttrryylloocckk() and pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__uunnlloocckk()
     functions will fail if:

     [EINVAL]           The value specified by _l_o_c_k is invalid or is not ini‐
                        tialized.

     The pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__lloocckk() function may fail if:

     [EDEADLK]          The calling thread already owns the lock.

     The pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__ttrryylloocckk() function will fail if:

     [EBUSY]            Another thread currently holds _l_o_c_k.

     The pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__uunnlloocckk() function may fail if:

     [EPERM]            The calling thread does not own _l_o_c_k.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     pthread_spin_destroy(3), pthread_spin_init(3)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__lloocckk(), pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__ttrryylloocckk() and pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__uunnlloocckk()
     functions first appeared in N:M Threading Library (libkse, -lkse) in
     FreeBSD 5.2, and in 1:1 Threading Library (libthr, -lthr) in FreeBSD 5.3.

BBUUGGSS
     The implementation of pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__lloocckk(), pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__ttrryylloocckk() and
     pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__uunnlloocckk() is expected to conform to IEEE Std 1003.2
     (“POSIX.2”).

